disparage the project, or imply that the licensor endorses you or **your
company**.

## Permitted Purposes & Anti-Resale Perimeter

Any commercial or noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose, **except** that
neither you nor **your company** may do any of the following:

1. **Standalone Resale or Hosted Cloud Services:** Sell, license for a fee, or
   offer to others as a hosted, managed, or multi-tenant cloud service (whether
   paid, credit-based, ad-supported, or free):
   - a rebranded, white-labeled, or repackaged version of the standalone
     reference plugin (`packages/plugin`), trainer (`packages/trainer`), or web
     studio (`packages/web`) whose primary value is substantially the software
     itself;
   - any automated or self-serve cloud training, capture-processing, or
     model-generation service or API powered by the software; or
   - any multi-creator or subscription cloud/browser audio-rendering or
     model-streaming service;
2. **Unlicensed Model Marketplaces:** Operate or power any **model marketplace**
   (whether commercial, ad-supported, subscription-based, or free), use any part
   of the software (including `dnam-engine`, its Python, JavaScript, or
   WebAssembly bindings, its container schemas, or its provenance, watermarking,
   ingestion-scanning, and `marketplace_receipt` tools) to run or support a
   **model marketplace**, or integrate any hardware device, plugin, or
   application using the software with an unlicensed **model marketplace**,
   without a separate written marketplace license from the licensor;
3. **Model Conversion, Distillation, or Unauthorized Redistribution:** Use the
   software (or provide any tool or service using the software) for format
   conversion, black-box distillation, or synthetic probe re-capture of someone
   else's `.dnam` or `.dnam-ckpt` models into another format, or extract or
   redistribute someone else's models in violation of the license terms in their
   `metadata.license` or `marketplace_receipt`, without that creator's
   permission; or
4. **White-Labeling or Circumvention:** Provide any hardware, firmware, plugin,
   or software that violates [Mandatory DNAM Branding & Format
   Integrity](#mandatory-dnam-branding--format-integrity).

### Individual Creator Model Publishing, Direct Sales & Audio Output

These terms do not restrict you from training, publishing, or selling **your own
models** individually, or from using the software in music and audio production:

- **Local, Personal Cloud & Studio Client Training:** You may run
  `packages/trainer` and `dnam-engine` on your own computers or on single-tenant
  cloud GPUs that you rent for your own use (such as personal Google Colab,
  RunPod, AWS, or Lambda Labs sessions) to train **your own models**. Studio
  engineers and producers may also capture and train custom `.dnam` models for
  individual clients as part of hands-on studio production or sound-design work.
- **Model Ownership & Direct Sales:** You keep full ownership of **your own
  models** (and may sign them with `creator_signature`) and may publish them for
  free or sell them directly to users—including on your own website, your own
  code repositories (such as GitHub), your own first-party storefront on
  general-purpose e-commerce and creator platforms (such as Shopify, Gumroad,
  Bandcamp, Lemon Squeezy, Payhip, Ko-fi, or Patreon), or bundled with your own
  compliant hardware devices or audio plugins—without paying any fee or royalty
  to the licensor. You may also embed `@dnam-project/engine` (WebAssembly
  `AudioWorklet`) on your own website so visitors can audition **your own
  models**.
- **Unrestricted Audio Output:** You keep full ownership of all audio
  recordings, performances, stems, and mixes you produce using the software or
  `.dnam` models, with no royalties or restrictions.

