## Definitions

The **licensor** is the individual or entity offering these terms, and the
**software** is the software (including code, binaries, schemas, container
specifications, and documentation) the licensor makes available under these
terms.

**You** refers to the individual or entity agreeing to these terms.

**Your company** is any legal entity, sole proprietorship, or other kind of
organization that you work for, plus all organizations that have control over,
are under the control of, or are under common control with that organization.
**Control** means ownership of substantially all the assets of an entity, or
the power to direct its management and policies by vote, contract, or
otherwise. Control can be direct or indirect.

**Your own models** are `.dnam` or `.dnam-ckpt` models that you (or your
company, including genuine studio collaborations) originally captured and
trained for your own first-party catalog, rather than models sourced,
aggregated, consigned, or sublicensed from multiple independent third-party
creators.

**Model marketplace** means any marketplace, multi-vendor storefront, model
exchange, tone-sharing repository, aggregator, publisher or consignment catalog,
or in-app, in-plugin, or companion-app cloud library that hosts, distributes,
brokers, streams, auditions, or sells `.dnam` or `.dnam-ckpt` models (or indexes
or curates them as a model directory or storefront) from multiple third-party
creators.

**Your licenses** are all the licenses granted to you for the software under
these terms.

**Use** means anything you do with the software requiring one of your licenses.
